🚽 sim.brainrot — the simulation, one step at a time.
🚽
🚽 This file could not exist until recently. A helper needs to see both an
🚽 entity and the shared world state, and the semantic analyser checked
🚽 struct-pointer parameters against a REVERSED parameter list: it rejected
🚽 `step(gang Ent *e, gang World *w)` called correctly, and accepted the
🚽 swapped call, which then wrote one struct's field offsets through the
🚽 other's pointer. DESIGN.md section 14.1 explains why the whole frame
🚽 loop lived in `skibidi main` because of it.
🚽
🚽 Fixed upstream in Brainrotlang/brainrot#294, so the extraction the design
🚽 doc promised would be mechanical is exactly that.
🚽
🚽 What is still in `main`, and why: the pool LOOPS. A struct field cannot
🚽 be an array of structs, so there is no God-struct to hand over, and
🚽 there is no pointer arithmetic on struct pointers, so a helper cannot
🚽 walk a pool itself. It can only be handed one already-resolved
🚽 `&pool[i]`. See DESIGN.md 15.2, C4 and C5.

gang World {
    chad dt;
    chad speed;
    chad dist;
    rizz bonus;
    rizz combo;
    chad spawn_t;
    rizz prev_kind;
    rizz next_kind;
    rizz seed;
    🚽 Each boss fires once per run. Tracked here rather than on the Boss
    🚽 itself, which is cleared the moment a fight ends and would forget.
    cap  did_tralalero;
    cap  did_bombardiro;
    cap  did_dimdim;
    cap  did_combinasion;
    🚽 Tung's live horizontal position, mirrored here each frame so a boss
    🚽 that runs its own machine (combi_move) can teleport relative to him
    🚽 without threading a Player pointer through boss_tick(). Equals
    🚽 t_player_x() in every mode except the Combinasion fight.
    chad tung_x;
};

gang Player {
    chad y;
    chad vy;
    cap  grounded;
    chad atk_t;
    chad iframe_t;
    rizz hearts;
    🚽 Horizontal position. Pinned at t_player_x() for the whole game EXCEPT
    🚽 the La Grande Combinasion fight, which unpins it (12.6.2). Only the
    🚽 combi_* functions and the player draw read it; everything else uses the
    🚽 t_player_x() constant, so it equals the constant in every other mode.
    chad x;
    🚽 Distance walked HORIZONTALLY, accumulated by player_move_x. In the still
    🚽 Combinasion arena the world does not scroll, so the run cycle is driven
    🚽 by this instead of world distance (walk_frame). Unused elsewhere.
    chad walk_t;
};

gang Ent {
    chad x;
    chad y;
    chad w;
    chad h;
    rizz kind;
    cap  alive;
};

🚽 A boss is not an Ent and does not live in a pool. It has phases, a bonk
🚽 count and scripted movement that no generic entity wants, and putting it
🚽 in `enemies[]` would drag all of that through the shared collision
🚽 passes. One boss is up at a time, so it is a single value.
🚽
🚽 Width and height come from the kind (boss_w / boss_h) rather than being
🚽 stored, so there is exactly one place a boss's size is written down.
gang Boss {
    rizz kind;
    rizz phase;
    rizz bonks;
    🚽 What it spawned last, so its own gaps can go through fair_clamp()
    🚽 exactly like the world spawner's do.
    rizz prev_kind;
    🚽 Damage the PLAYER has taken this fight. Tralalero closes on it.
    rizz hits;
    chad x;
    chad y;
    chad phase_t;
    chad spawn_t;
    🚽 U Din Din's charge direction: +1 = left-to-right, -1 = right-to-left.
    🚽 La Grande Combinasion reuses it as facing (+1 faces right, -1 left).
    🚽 Unused by the other two bosses.
    rizz dir;
    🚽 La Grande Combinasion only (12.6). His sub-state (t_cs_*), the exact x
    🚽 his teleport tell promised (materialise lands here), and how many swings
    🚽 into the current chain he is. prev_kind doubles as his teleport counter
    🚽 (he spawns nothing, so its fair_clamp meaning is free). Unused by others.
    rizz state;
    chad dest_x;
    rizz script_i;
};

🚽 Bombardiro's ordnance. Falls under the same gravity the player does,
🚽 then sits as a ground blast for t_bomb_fuse() seconds. `fuse > 0.0` is
🚽 what distinguishes the two states -- a landed bomb is not a separate
🚽 pool, it is the same slot with a different box and a countdown.
gang Bomb {
    chad x;
    chad y;
    chad vy;
    🚽 Seconds until impact. Kept rather than re-derived because recovering
    🚽 it from y and vy needs a square root, and the landing marker wants it
    🚽 every frame.
    chad fall_t;
    chad fuse;
    cap  alive;
};

🚽 --- world ---------------------------------------------------------------

skibidi world_reset(gang World *w) {
    w.speed     = t_speed_start();
    w.dist      = 0.0;
    w.bonus     = 0;
    w.combo     = 0;
    w.spawn_t   = 1.2;
    w.prev_kind = t_kind_patapim();
    w.did_tralalero  = L;
    w.did_bombardiro = L;
    w.did_dimdim     = L;
    w.did_combinasion = L;
    w.tung_x         = t_player_x();
}

🚽 One variable drives the whole game (DESIGN.md section 7). The cap is
🚽 story mode's; endless mode removes it.
skibidi world_advance(gang World *w) {
    w.speed = w.speed + t_speed_accel() * w.dt;
    edgy (w.speed > t_speed_max()) { w.speed = t_speed_max(); }
    w.dist = w.dist + w.speed * w.dt;
}

🚽 Distance is worth a tenth of a point; bonks are worth the rest.
🚽
🚽 This used to route through a truncf() helper, because assigning a bare
🚽 chad variable to a rizz reinterpreted the float's bit pattern instead of
🚽 converting it -- 17.5 became 1099694080. Fixed upstream in
🚽 Brainrotlang/brainrot#299, so the conversion is now just a conversion.
rizz world_score(gang World *w) {
    bussin w.dist * 0.1 + w.bonus;
}

🚽 --- player --------------------------------------------------------------

skibidi player_reset(gang Player *p) {
    p.y        = t_ground_y() - t_player_h();
    p.vy       = 0.0;
    p.grounded = W;
    p.atk_t    = 0.0;
    p.iframe_t = 0.0;
    p.hearts   = t_hearts_max();
    p.x        = t_player_x();
    p.walk_t   = 0.0;
}

🚽 Refused in mid-air, so holding the key cannot autohop.
🚽
🚽 Reports whether it actually launched. The caller needs that to fire the
🚽 jump sound only on a real jump -- keeping the decision here rather than
🚽 having main re-test `grounded` itself, which would be the same rule
🚽 written twice and free to drift.
cap player_jump(gang Player *p) {
    edgy (p.grounded) {
        p.vy       = t_jump_v();
        p.grounded = L;
        bussin W;
    }
    bussin L;
}

🚽 Refused during the 0.45s attack timer, which is what makes the last
🚽 0.30s of it a cooldown rather than a second swing.
skibidi player_swing(gang Player *p) {
    edgy (p.atk_t <= 0.0) { p.atk_t = t_attack_total(); }
}

skibidi player_physics(gang Player *p, gang World *w) {
    p.vy = p.vy + t_gravity() * w.dt;
    p.y  = p.y + p.vy * w.dt;
    chad floor_y = t_ground_y() - t_player_h();
    edgy (p.y > floor_y) {
        p.y        = floor_y;
        p.vy       = 0.0;
        p.grounded = W;
    }
}

skibidi player_tick_timers(gang Player *p, gang World *w) {
    edgy (p.atk_t > 0.0) {
        p.atk_t = p.atk_t - w.dt;
        edgy (p.atk_t < 0.0) { p.atk_t = 0.0; }
    }
    edgy (p.iframe_t > 0.0) {
        p.iframe_t = p.iframe_t - w.dt;
        edgy (p.iframe_t < 0.0) { p.iframe_t = 0.0; }
    }
}

🚽 The bat is live for the first 0.15s of the 0.45s timer.
cap player_swinging(gang Player *p) {
    bussin p.atk_t > t_attack_active();
}

cap player_vulnerable(gang Player *p) {
    bussin p.iframe_t <= 0.0;
}

🚽 A heart and the combo. Notably NOT the speed.
🚽
🚽 Damage used to knock the world speed back by a quarter, described as a
🚽 mercy and a punishment at once. It was neither. At 900 px/s it handed
🚽 back 225 px/s, which takes 75 seconds to climb again -- a quarter of a
🚽 whole run spent easier, bought for one of three hearts. That makes
🚽 deliberately eating a hit the CORRECT play at the top of the curve,
🚽 which is a strategy the game should not reward.
🚽
🚽 The mercy was redundant too: 1.2s of invulnerability is 1080px of
🚽 clearance at that speed, most of a screen, which is what actually saves
🚽 you from a second hit.
🚽
🚽 And it fought the first design pillar. The whole game is one number
🚽 rising; a hit that pushes it back down makes the curve non-monotonic and
🚽 turns failure into relief. Losing a third of your health and up to an
🚽 x8 combo is punishment enough.
skibidi player_take_hit(gang Player *p, gang World *w) {
    p.hearts   = p.hearts - 1;
    p.iframe_t = t_iframe_time();
    w.combo    = 0;
}

🚽 Flash on alternate 0.1s ticks while invulnerable.
cap player_visible(gang Player *p) {
    edgy (p.iframe_t <= 0.0) { bussin W; }
    rizz tick = p.iframe_t * 10.0;
    edgy (tick % 2 == 0) { bussin L; }
    bussin W;
}

🚽 --- animation -----------------------------------------------------------
🚽
🚽 Which frame to show is derived entirely from state the simulation already
🚽 keeps, so there is no animation clock to drift out of step with the game.

🚽 The run cycle advances with DISTANCE, not time. Tie it to a fixed frame
🚽 rate and the feet skate as soon as the world outruns it; tie it to ground
🚽 covered and they stay planted at every speed, which is the whole illusion
🚽 in a runner. It also means the cycle naturally quickens with the
🚽 difficulty curve without a second variable to tune.
rizz run_frame(gang World *w) {
    rizz i = w.dist / t_run_stride();
    bussin i % t_run_frames();
}

🚽 The same cycle, but driven by HORIZONTAL walk distance rather than world
🚽 scroll -- for the Combinasion fight, where the arena is frozen (12.6.2) so
🚽 w.dist does not move but Tung does. Same stride, so the cadence matches.
rizz walk_frame(gang Player *p) {
    rizz i = p.walk_t / t_run_stride();
    bussin i % t_run_frames();
}

🚽 Rising or falling, off the sign of vertical velocity.
rizz jump_frame(gang Player *p) {
    edgy (p.vy < 0.0) { bussin 0; }
    bussin 1;
}

🚽 Strike, recoil, return -- evenly across the 0.45s attack timer.
🚽
🚽 Frame 0 is the strike and it lands on the FIRST third, because that is
🚽 when the hitbox is live (atk_t above t_attack_active()). An animation
🚽 that wound up first would be showing a wind-up while the bat was already
🚽 hitting things.
rizz swing_frame(gang Player *p) {
    chad elapsed = t_attack_total() - p.atk_t;
    rizz i = elapsed / (t_attack_total() / t_swing_frames());
    edgy (i < 0) { bussin 0; }
    edgy (i >= t_swing_frames()) { bussin t_swing_frames() - 1; }
    bussin i;
}

🚽 Patapim's charge, on the same distance-driven principle as Tung's run --
🚽 but off the entity's OWN travel, not the world's, since it closes faster
🚽 than the ground scrolls (t_enemy_close()). Using world distance would
🚽 make its legs lag behind the body it is attached to.
rizz patapim_frame(gang Ent *e) {
    rizz i = (t_spawn_x() - e.x) / t_patapim_stride();
    edgy (i < 0) { i = 0 - i; }
    bussin i % t_patapim_frames();
}

🚽 Vaca Saturno's two-frame walk, off its own travel like Patapim's.
rizz vaca_frame(gang Ent *e) {
    rizz i = (t_spawn_x() - e.x) / t_vaca_stride();
    edgy (i < 0) { i = 0 - i; }
    bussin i % t_vaca_frames();
}


🚽 --- entities ------------------------------------------------------------

skibidi ent_spawn(gang Ent *e, rizz kind) {
    e.kind  = kind;
    e.w     = kind_w(kind);
    e.h     = kind_h(kind);
    e.x     = t_spawn_x();
    e.y     = t_ground_y() - kind_h(kind);
    e.alive = W;
}

🚽 `extra` is the closing speed on top of the world's: zero for obstacles,
🚽 ENEMY_CLOSE for enemies, so a Patapim arrives sooner than the spacing
🚽 suggests and cannot be pattern-memorised by gap alone.
🚽
🚽 Despawning off the left edge does NOT break the combo. Only getting hit
🚽 does, which keeps the incentive aggressive rather than cautious.
skibidi ent_scroll(gang Ent *e, gang World *w, chad extra) {
    e.x = e.x - (w.speed + extra) * w.dt;
    edgy (e.x < 0.0 - e.w) { e.alive = L; }
}

cap ent_hits_body(gang Ent *e, gang Player *p) {
    bussin aabb(t_player_x(), p.y, t_player_w(), t_player_h(),
                e.x, e.y, e.w, e.h);
}

cap ent_in_bat(gang Ent *e, gang Player *p) {
    bussin aabb(t_player_x() + t_hitbox_dx(), p.y + t_hitbox_dy(),
                t_hitbox_w(), t_hitbox_h(),
                e.x, e.y, e.w, e.h);
}

🚽 Consecutive bonks without taking damage, capped at x8.
skibidi award_bonk(gang World *w) {
    w.combo = w.combo + 1;
    edgy (w.combo > 8) { w.combo = 8; }
    w.bonus = w.bonus + 100 * w.combo;
}

🚽 --- pools ----------------------------------------------------------------
🚽
🚽 These could not exist until brainrot#311. A helper had no way to WALK a
🚽 pool -- there was no pointer arithmetic or indexing on struct pointers, so
🚽 it could only be handed one already-resolved `&pool[i]`, and every loop
🚽 had to live in `skibidi main`. DESIGN.md 14.1 called that "still forced".
🚽 It is not any more.
🚽
🚽 Each pass owns the ITERATION and the geometry. `main` keeps the response --
🚽 the sound, the scoring, the state change -- which is why these hand back a
🚽 count or a flag instead of reaching for the audio seam. Simulation never
🚽 draws and never plays; that split is what the headless harness relies on.

skibidi pool_clear(gang Ent *pool, rizz n) {
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) { pool[i].alive = L; }
}

🚽 The first free slot, or -1. A full pool silently skips the spawn, and that
🚽 is correct behaviour rather than an error -- the gap still advances.
rizz pool_free_slot(gang Ent *pool, rizz n) {
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) {
        edgy (!pool[i].alive) { bussin i; }
    }
    bussin 0 - 1;
}

skibidi pool_scroll(gang Ent *pool, rizz n, gang World *w, chad extra) {
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) {
        edgy (pool[i].alive) { ent_scroll(&pool[i], w, extra); }
    }
}

🚽 How many the bat connected with. Plural on purpose: two enemies can sit
🚽 inside the hitbox at once and both should score.
rizz pool_bat_pass(gang Ent *pool, rizz n, gang Player *p, gang World *w) {
    rizz bonks = 0;
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) {
        edgy (pool[i].alive) {
            cap bonk = ent_in_bat(&pool[i], p);
            edgy (bonk) {
                pool[i].alive = L;
                award_bonk(w);
                bonks = bonks + 1;
            }
        }
    }
    bussin bonks;
}

🚽 A `cap`-returning call can be a condition directly since brainrot#324,
🚽 and the pure predicates in this file now are. The ones still landing in a
🚽 named local first -- this one, pool_bat_pass(), player_jump() -- do it on
🚽 purpose: they have side effects. A call that kills entities and damages
🚽 the player does not belong hidden inside an `edgy (...)`, where nothing
🚽 warns the reader that evaluating the condition changed the world.
🚽
🚽 Did the player take a hit? At most one per frame in practice --
🚽 player_take_hit() starts the iframes that make every later check fail --
🚽 but the vulnerability is re-read per entity rather than assumed, because
🚽 that is what makes the "at most one" true rather than hoped for.
cap pool_body_pass(gang Ent *pool, rizz n, gang Player *p, gang World *w) {
    cap hurt = L;
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) {
        edgy (pool[i].alive) {
            cap open = player_vulnerable(p);
            edgy (open) {
                edgy (ent_hits_body(&pool[i], p)) {
                    pool[i].alive = L;
                    player_take_hit(p, w);
                    hurt = W;
                }
            }
        }
    }
    bussin hurt;
}

🚽 --- bomb pool ------------------------------------------------------------
🚽 Its own set, because gang Bomb is its own type -- there is still no
🚽 generic over two struct types.

skibidi bombs_clear(gang Bomb *pool, rizz n) {
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) {
        pool[i].alive  = L;
        pool[i].fall_t = 0.0;
    }
}

rizz bombs_free_slot(gang Bomb *pool, rizz n) {
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) {
        edgy (!pool[i].alive) { bussin i; }
    }
    bussin 0 - 1;
}

🚽 Returns how many bombs hit the ground THIS frame, so main can sound the
🚽 impact (the blast landing, distinct from the player being hit by it).
rizz bombs_step(gang Bomb *pool, rizz n, gang World *w) {
    rizz landed = 0;
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) {
        edgy (pool[i].alive) {
            cap hit = bomb_tick(&pool[i], w);
            edgy (hit) { landed = landed + 1; }
        }
    }
    bussin landed;
}

🚽 The blast is NOT consumed by the hit. It is a hazard sitting on the
🚽 ground, not a projectile, and the iframes already stop it draining more
🚽 than one heart.
cap bombs_body_pass(gang Bomb *pool, rizz n, gang Player *p, gang World *w) {
    cap hurt = L;
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) {
        edgy (pool[i].alive) {
            cap open = player_vulnerable(p);
            edgy (open) {
                cap blast = bomb_hits_player(&pool[i], p);
                edgy (blast) {
                    player_take_hit(p, w);
                    hurt = W;
                }
            }
        }
    }
    bussin hurt;
}

🚽 --- bosses --------------------------------------------------------------
🚽
🚽 DESIGN.md section 12. Tralalero and Bombardiro are set pieces, not
🚽 generic enemies, and they share one shape:
🚽
🚽     survive a phase -> an opening appears -> one bonk -> repeat x3
🚽
🚽 While a boss is up the normal spawner is paused and the boss owns the
🚽 pattern. You can still die the ordinary way, hearts and all -- a boss
🚽 fight is a harder stretch of the same game, not a separate mode.
🚽

chad boss_w(rizz kind) {
    edgy (kind == t_boss_tralalero()) { bussin t_shark_w(); }
    edgy (kind == t_boss_dimdim()) { bussin t_dindin_w(); }
    edgy (kind == t_boss_combinasion()) { bussin t_combi_w(); }
    bussin t_croc_w();
}

chad boss_h(rizz kind) {
    edgy (kind == t_boss_tralalero()) { bussin t_shark_h(); }
    edgy (kind == t_boss_dimdim()) { bussin t_dindin_h(); }
    edgy (kind == t_boss_combinasion()) { bussin t_combi_h(); }
    bussin t_croc_h();
}

skibidi boss_clear(gang Boss *b) {
    b.kind    = t_boss_none();
    b.phase   = t_boss_off();
    b.bonks   = 0;
    b.hits    = 0;
    b.x       = 0.0;
    b.y       = 0.0;
    b.phase_t = 0.0;
    b.spawn_t = 0.0;
    b.prev_kind = t_kind_crate();
    b.dir     = 0;
    b.state   = t_cs_out();
    b.dest_x  = 0.0;
    b.script_i = 0;
}

cap boss_active(gang Boss *b) {
    bussin b.kind != t_boss_none();
}

🚽 Does the boss own the spawner this frame? True for the whole fight
🚽 except the exit, so the normal curve resumes while he is still sliding
🚽 off screen rather than leaving a dead beat behind him.
cap boss_owns_spawner(gang Boss *b) {
    bussin b.kind != t_boss_none() && b.phase != t_boss_leave();
}

🚽 The lead a bomb released RIGHT NOW would give Tung: the seconds between
🚽 the blast appearing on the ground and its leading edge reaching his front.
🚽 Everything about a fair drop is expressed in this one number.
🚽
🚽 Three boxes deep, and each offset is a real one rather than a fudge. The
🚽 shell leaves the middle of the bay (bomb_spawn), the blast is centred on
🚽 where the shell was and is wider than it (bomb_tick), and the blast then
🚽 scrolls left at world speed while Tung stays pinned at t_player_x().
chad croc_bomb_lead(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    chad shell = b.x + (t_croc_w() - t_bomb_w()) * 0.5;
    chad blast = shell - (t_blast_w() - t_bomb_w()) * 0.5;
    bussin (blast - (t_player_x() + t_player_w())) / w.speed;
}

🚽 Where the croc holds station while bombing -- read backwards out of
🚽 croc_bomb_lead(), so the column is a CONSEQUENCE of where the bombs have
🚽 to land rather than a number someone liked the look of. Move t_bomb_lead()
🚽 and he moves with it.
chad croc_cruise_x(gang World *w, chad lead) {
    chad blast = t_player_x() + t_player_w() + w.speed * lead;
    chad shell = blast + (t_blast_w() - t_bomb_w()) * 0.5;
    bussin shell - (t_croc_w() - t_bomb_w()) * 0.5;
}

🚽 May the boss release its pattern this frame?
🚽
🚽 Tralalero always can -- he throws obstacles, and those enter at
🚽 t_spawn_x() off the right edge whatever he is doing. The croc is the one
🚽 that can say no, and he says it for two different reasons.
🚽
🚽 ALTITUDE. bomb_gravity() is derived from ONE drop: the bay at
🚽 t_croc_cruise_y() + t_croc_h() down to the ground. A shell released lower
🚽 has less air to fall through -- and at the opening he is at
🚽 t_croc_open_y(), which puts the bay at 542 while the ground trigger is
🚽 534. The bomb was already past its own landing line on the frame it was
🚽 created, so it detonated in one tick: no arc, no fall, no marker, a blast
🚽 out of nothing. That is what "not following the laws of physics" was.
🚽
🚽 COLUMN. A bomb released short of t_bomb_lead_min() lands on or next to
🚽 Tung, and a falling shell keeps its column while Tung cannot move -- so
🚽 that bomb is unavoidable rather than difficult. See t_bomb_lead().
🚽
🚽 Both cases are the SAME moment: the dive to the opening and the climb back
🚽 out, when he is low and near Tung's column. He holds his fire crossing
🚽 that ground, which reads -- jaws open and diving is not a bombing run.
🚽
🚽 Altitude is `<=` because higher is only ever more fall time, and
🚽 approach() lands exactly on its target so the cruise case is exact.
cap boss_may_spawn(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    edgy (b.kind != t_boss_bombardiro()) { bussin W; }
    edgy (b.y > t_croc_cruise_y()) { bussin L; }
    chad lead = croc_bomb_lead(b, w);
    bussin lead >= t_bomb_lead_min();
}

🚽 Only during the opening, and only until the third bonk lands.
🚽
🚽 La Grande Combinasion has no `open` phase -- his opening is the RECOVERY
🚽 after a whiffed swing, and it is the only window he can be damaged in.
cap boss_vulnerable(gang Boss *b) {
    edgy (b.kind == t_boss_combinasion()) {
        bussin b.state == t_cs_recover() && b.bonks < t_boss_bonks();
    }
    bussin b.phase == t_boss_open() && b.bonks < t_boss_bonks();
}

🚽 Which boss, if any, this LEVEL has just earned. The shark is checked
🚽 first so a run that somehow crosses both thresholds while one is already
🚽 up still takes them in order rather than skipping him.
🚽
🚽 Level rather than score: see t_tralalero_lvl() for why. Score is not a
🚽 measure of progress here, it is a measure of how well you are playing.
rizz boss_due(gang World *w, rizz lvl) {
    edgy (!w.did_tralalero && lvl >= t_tralalero_lvl()) {
        bussin t_boss_tralalero();
    }
    edgy (!w.did_bombardiro && lvl >= t_bombardiro_lvl()) {
        bussin t_boss_bombardiro();
    }
    edgy (!w.did_dimdim && lvl >= t_dindin_lvl()) {
        bussin t_boss_dimdim();
    }
    🚽 The true final boss: only once U Din Din is beaten (did_dimdim set), so
    🚽 he arrives the moment the story cap dies -- the run the player thought
    🚽 they had won just keeps going (12.6). Same LVL 9 gate; no higher level
    🚽 exists (t_speed_max caps at LVL 9), so this reads off did_dimdim.
    edgy (!w.did_combinasion && w.did_dimdim && lvl >= t_dindin_lvl()) {
        bussin t_boss_combinasion();
    }
    bussin t_boss_none();
}

skibidi boss_start(gang Boss *b, gang World *w, rizz kind) {
    b.kind    = kind;
    b.phase   = t_boss_survive();
    b.bonks   = 0;
    b.hits    = 0;
    b.phase_t = 0.0;
    b.spawn_t = 0.0;
    b.prev_kind = t_kind_crate();

    🚽 Enter from where he lives, so the approach is visible rather than a
    🚽 pop-in: the shark from off the left edge, the croc from overhead.
    edgy (kind == t_boss_tralalero()) {
        🚽 Start reared back at the left edge with a telegraph before the
        🚽 first charge -- spawn_t is the charge timer here, not a spawner one.
        b.x = t_shark_charge_x0();
        b.y = t_ground_y() - t_shark_h();
        b.spawn_t = t_shark_charge_gap();
        w.did_tralalero = W;
    }
    amogus {
        edgy (kind == t_boss_dimdim()) {
            🚽 Start in the tremble phase; dindin_move()'s fresh-entry sets up
            🚽 the first charge. dir = +1 so the first flip makes it -1
            🚽 (right-to-left) -- his opening charge comes from the right.
            b.phase   = t_boss_survive();
            b.dir     = 1;
            b.spawn_t = 0.0;
            b.x       = t_screen_w();
            b.y       = t_ground_y() - t_dindin_h();
            w.did_dimdim = W;
        }
        amogus {
            edgy (kind == t_boss_combinasion()) {
                🚽 Enters by teleporting in: start OUT (invisible) at centre,
                🚽 off the top so the primitive fallback is not parked mid-arena
                🚽 during the blank. The first tell places him near Tung. He
                🚽 runs his own machine (combi_move); phase stays `survive` so he
                🚽 owns the spawner (and never spawns), flipping to `leave` only
                🚽 when the third bonk lands.
                b.state    = t_cs_out();
                b.script_i = 0;
                b.prev_kind = 0;   🚽 teleport counter (see combi_pick_dest)
                b.dir      = 1;
                b.x        = t_screen_w() / 2.0;
                b.y        = t_ground_y() - t_combi_h();
                b.dest_x   = b.x;
                w.did_combinasion = W;
            }
            amogus {
                b.x = croc_cruise_x(w, t_bomb_lead());
                b.y = t_croc_cruise_y();
                w.did_bombardiro = W;
            }
        }
    }
}

🚽 How far back the shark lurks, given the mistakes made this fight.
🚽
🚽 Clamped so his nose stops t_shark_close_min() short of Tung's back. The
🚽 closing is dread, not damage: the player cannot move horizontally, so a
🚽 boss that walks into them is unavoidable damage rather than difficulty.
chad boss_lurk_x(gang Boss *b) {
    chad want = t_shark_lurk_x() + b.hits * t_shark_close_step();
    chad most = t_player_x() - t_shark_close_min() - t_shark_w();
    bussin minf(want, most);
}

🚽 Which side of Tung is a box of width `w` sitting at `x` on?
🚽 -1 behind him, +1 in front of him, 0 overlapping his column.
rizz boss_side(chad x, chad w) {
    edgy (x + w < t_player_x()) { bussin 0 - 1; }
    edgy (x > t_player_x() + t_player_w()) { bussin 1; }
    bussin 0;
}

🚽 May the boss move horizontally this frame without ending up inside Tung?
🚽
🚽 THIS is the rule that keeps a boss fight fair. The player is pinned at
🚽 t_player_x() and can only jump, so a boss that slides through them is
🚽 contact nobody can dodge -- and the bosses have to cross, because their
🚽 openings are in FRONT of Tung (that is the only place the bat reaches)
🚽 while Tralalero chases from BEHIND.
🚽
🚽 So every horizontal move is gated: either the boss is clear above Tung's
🚽 head, or it is already on the side it is heading for and is not crossing
🚽 at all. Combined with a vertical move that runs FIRST, that makes the
🚽 leap lead the crossing -- rise in place, cross overhead, come down on the
🚽 far side. Moving both axes together does not work: at t_boss_move_speed()
🚽 a boss climbs exactly as fast as it advances, so it is still half-way up
🚽 when it arrives, and clips through.
cap boss_may_advance(gang Boss *b, chad target_x) {
    chad w = boss_w(b.kind);
    cap clear_above = b.y + boss_h(b.kind) < t_ground_y() - t_player_h();
    edgy (clear_above) { bussin W; }
    rizz here = boss_side(b.x, w);
    rizz want = boss_side(target_x, w);
    bussin here != 0 && here == want;
}

🚽 Where the boss wants to be right now -- a pure function of (kind, phase,
🚽 hits, dist), so an opening always arrives at the same place and the bat
🚽 ranges written into tune.brainrot stay meaningful.
chad boss_target_x(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    🚽 Beaten: off the left edge, and far enough that the clamp in
    🚽 boss_lurk_x() cannot pull him back.
    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_leave()) { bussin 0.0 - t_screen_w(); }

    edgy (b.kind == t_boss_tralalero()) {
        edgy (b.phase == t_boss_open()) { bussin t_shark_open_x(); }
        bussin boss_lurk_x(b);
    }
    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_open()) { bussin t_croc_open_x(); }

    🚽 He flies AHEAD of Tung, not over him, and the distance is whatever
    🚽 t_bomb_lead() seconds of scroll comes to at the current speed. A bomb
    🚽 released over Tung's own column is welded to him -- see t_bomb_lead().
    🚽
    🚽 The sway is on the LEAD, so it wanders in seconds rather than pixels
    🚽 and stays inside the same fairness window at every speed. That is what
    🚽 keeps the arrivals off a metronome.
    🚽
    🚽 He is still the source of his own bombs and still directly above every
    🚽 marker he draws, which is what "I can't see where the bombs are coming
    🚽 from" actually asked for -- the guide line goes straight down from him.
    chad lead = t_bomb_lead()
                + wave(w.dist * 0.001 * t_croc_sway_rate()) * t_bomb_lead_sway();
    bussin croc_cruise_x(w, lead);
}

chad boss_target_y(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    chad high = t_ground_y() - t_player_h() - boss_h(b.kind) - 8.0;

    🚽 Beaten: launched. Three bat hits put him in the air, and it is also
    🚽 what stops a defeated boss sliding back through Tung on the way out.
    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_leave()) { bussin high - t_boss_leave_rise(); }

    edgy (b.kind == t_boss_tralalero()) {
        chad ground = t_ground_y() - t_shark_h();
        🚽 Airborne while he is on a different side of Tung than he is
        🚽 heading for -- which includes overlapping him (side 0).
        🚽
        🚽 Deliberately NOT phrased as "while boss_may_advance() is false":
        🚽 that is circular. Rising makes may_advance true, which would make
        🚽 the target the ground again, which drops him, which makes it
        🚽 false. He hovered and never crossed.
        rizz here = boss_side(b.x, t_shark_w());
        rizz want = boss_side(boss_target_x(b, w), t_shark_w());
        edgy (here != want) { bussin high; }
        bussin ground;
    }

    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_open()) { bussin t_croc_open_y(); }
    bussin t_croc_cruise_y();
}

skibidi boss_move(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    chad speed = t_boss_move_speed();
    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_leave()) { speed = t_boss_leave_speed(); }
    chad step = speed * w.dt;

    🚽 Vertical first, so the leap leads -- see boss_may_advance().
    b.y = approach(b.y, boss_target_y(b, w), step);

    chad tx = boss_target_x(b, w);
    cap go = boss_may_advance(b, tx);
    edgy (go) { b.x = approach(b.x, tx, step); }
}

🚽 Has the boss finished moving to where its phase wants it?
cap boss_in_position(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    bussin absf(b.x - boss_target_x(b, w)) < 1.0
        && absf(b.y - boss_target_y(b, w)) < 1.0;
}

🚽 The phase machine. Survive for a fixed stretch, open for a short one,
🚽 and go back to surviving if the window closes unpunished -- a missed
🚽 opening costs time, not health, so the fight is long rather than unfair.
🚽
🚽 The opening's clock does NOT start until the boss has arrived, and that
🚽 is the difference between a fight and a coin flip. Tralalero spends 0.78s
🚽 of his lunge rising, crossing over Tung and coming down; when the timer
🚽 ran from the start of the phase, only the last 14 frames of a 61-frame
🚽 window had him inside bat reach. A player reacting to "he is open!"
🚽 swung immediately, hit nothing, and t_attack_total()'s 0.45s cooldown
🚽 then ate the only part that counted. Starting the clock on arrival gives
🚽 the whole t_boss_open_time() with him actually there.
skibidi boss_tick(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    edgy (b.kind == t_boss_none()) { bussin; }

    🚽 U Din Din runs his own state machine (tremble/charge/leave) in
    🚽 dindin_move(), not the shared survive->open->survive timing. phase_t is
    🚽 just his animation clock here.
    edgy (b.kind == t_boss_dimdim()) {
        b.phase_t = b.phase_t + w.dt;
        dindin_move(b, w);
        bussin;
    }

    🚽 La Grande Combinasion likewise runs his own machine (TELEPORT -> WINDUP
    🚽 -> SWING -> RECOVERY) in combi_move(), not the shared survive/open timer.
    edgy (b.kind == t_boss_combinasion()) {
        combi_move(b, w);
        bussin;
    }

    cap ticking = W;
    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_open()) { ticking = boss_in_position(b, w); }
    edgy (ticking) { b.phase_t = b.phase_t + w.dt; }

    🚽 Tralalero's survive phase is his own charge loop, not the generic
    🚽 approach-to-target move. Every other case (his opening cross, his
    🚽 leave, and the whole croc fight) still uses boss_move().
    edgy (b.kind == t_boss_tralalero() && b.phase == t_boss_survive()) {
        shark_charge_move(b, w);
    }
    amogus {
        edgy (b.kind == t_boss_tralalero() && b.phase == t_boss_open()) {
            shark_open_move(b, w);
        }
        amogus {
            boss_move(b, w);
        }
    }

    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_leave()) {
        edgy (b.phase_t >= t_boss_leave_time()) { boss_clear(b); }
        bussin;
    }

    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_survive()) {
        edgy (b.phase_t >= t_boss_survive_time()) {
            b.phase   = t_boss_open();
            b.phase_t = 0.0;
            🚽 Tralalero winds up before the lunge: retreat behind Tung and
            🚽 seed the vertical-bob tell (spawn_t), which shark_open_move()
            🚽 plays before crossing to the front.
            edgy (b.kind == t_boss_tralalero()) {
                b.x       = t_shark_charge_x0();
                b.y       = t_ground_y() - t_shark_h();
                b.spawn_t = t_shark_lunge_tell();
            }
        }
        bussin;
    }

    edgy (b.phase_t >= t_boss_open_time()) {
        b.phase   = t_boss_survive();
        b.phase_t = 0.0;
        🚽 Missed opening: re-telegraph the next charge (Tralalero only).
        edgy (b.kind == t_boss_tralalero()) { b.spawn_t = t_shark_charge_gap(); }
    }
}

🚽 --- Tralalero's charge (survive phase) ---------------------------------
🚽 He waits reared at the left edge (spawn_t counting down = the telegraph),
🚽 then sweeps right across the whole screen, low on the ground. The player
🚽 jumps the pass. Off the right edge he loops back to the start and rears
🚽 again. Uses only b.x, b.y and b.spawn_t -- no struct change, and no world
🚽 spawner (main clears the field and spawns nothing during his fight).
skibidi shark_charge_move(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    b.y = t_ground_y() - t_shark_h();
    edgy (b.spawn_t > 0.0) {
        b.spawn_t = b.spawn_t - w.dt;
        🚽 Anticipation tell: rear back + shudder, both harder as the launch
        🚽 nears (grow runs 0 -> 1 across the telegraph). He is off the left
        🚽 edge, far from Tung, so this x wobble is cosmetic wind-up only.
        chad into = t_shark_charge_gap() - b.spawn_t;      🚽 time into the tell
        chad grow = into / t_shark_charge_gap();           🚽 0 at start, ~1 at launch
        chad shake = wave(into * t_shark_tell_rate())
                     * t_shark_tell_shake() * grow;
        b.x = t_shark_charge_x0() - t_shark_tell_rear() * grow + shake;
        bussin;
    }
    b.x = b.x + t_shark_charge_speed() * w.dt;
    edgy (b.x > t_screen_w()) {
        b.x       = t_shark_charge_x0();
        b.spawn_t = t_shark_charge_gap();
    }
}

🚽 Tralalero's open phase. First a VERTICAL wind-up (spawn_t, seeded on the
🚽 survive->open flip): he waits behind Tung's column and bobs up and down,
🚽 harder as it runs down, telegraphing the lunge. Then boss_move() carries
🚽 the actual cross to the front -- rising over Tung (the "don't jump" beat)
🚽 and parking at t_shark_open_x() for the bonk window.
skibidi shark_open_move(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    edgy (b.spawn_t > 0.0) {
        b.spawn_t = b.spawn_t - w.dt;
        chad into = t_shark_lunge_tell() - b.spawn_t;
        chad grow = into / t_shark_lunge_tell();
        🚽 (0.5 + 0.5*wave) keeps the bob ABOVE the ground rest -- up and back,
        🚽 never clipping down through the floor.
        chad bob  = t_shark_lunge_bob() * grow
                    * (0.5 + 0.5 * wave(into * t_shark_tell_rate()));
        b.x = t_shark_charge_x0();
        b.y = t_ground_y() - t_shark_h() - bob;
        bussin;
    }
    boss_move(b, w);
}

🚽 The low charge's collision box: a jumpable band (t_shark_charge_h) on the
🚽 ground under the shark, not his full sprite -- see t_shark_charge_h().
cap shark_low_hits(gang Boss *b, gang Player *p) {
    bussin aabb(t_player_x(), p.y, t_player_w(), t_player_h(),
                b.x, t_ground_y() - t_shark_charge_h(),
                t_shark_w(), t_shark_charge_h());
}

🚽 The overhead cross box: his full sprite, up at head height during the
🚽 lunge to the front (b.y raised above the ground line).
cap shark_high_hits(gang Boss *b, gang Player *p) {
    bussin aabb(t_player_x(), p.y, t_player_w(), t_player_h(),
                b.x, b.y, t_shark_w(), t_shark_h());
}

🚽 Tralalero's body is the threat (unlike the croc, whose body never touches
🚽 -- see boss_hits_body). But ONLY in a dodgeable state, and the two states
🚽 are phase-separated so there is never a frame where both would hit:
🚽   survive: he charges LOW  -> jump it   (grounded + overlap = hit)
🚽   open:    he crosses HIGH -> duck it   (airborne + overlap = hit),
🚽            and only while raised mid-cross; once parked in front at ground
🚽            level he no longer overlaps Tung's column, so the bonk window is
🚽            contact-safe.
🚽 That "always exactly one safe input during an overlap" is the fairness
🚽 invariant unit_boss asserts, replacing the old "body never overlaps at all".
cap shark_contact_hit(gang Boss *b, gang Player *p) {
    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_survive()) {
        bussin p.grounded && shark_low_hits(b, p);
    }
    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_open()) {
        cap crossing = b.y < t_ground_y() - t_shark_h() - 1.0;
        bussin crossing && !p.grounded && shark_high_hits(b, p);
    }
    bussin L;
}

🚽 --- U Din Din's charge (final boss) -------------------------------------
🚽 He alternates sides: tremble at one edge (the tell), then sweep the whole
🚽 screen across. Off the far edge he trembles on THAT side and charges back.
🚽 `dir` is the sweep direction (+1 right, -1 left); spawn_t times the tremble,
🚽 phase_t drives the run-cycle animation (both here, not the generic phase
🚽 machine -- boss_tick() routes dimdim straight to this). He is always low, so
🚽 a jump always clears him; standing to swing is the risk.
skibidi dindin_move(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    b.y = t_ground_y() - t_dindin_h();

    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_leave()) {
        🚽 Launched out the way he was last heading, fast, then gone.
        b.x = b.x + b.dir * t_dindin_charge_speed() * 1.6 * w.dt;
        edgy (b.x < 0.0 - t_dindin_w() || b.x > t_screen_w() + t_dindin_w()) {
            boss_clear(b);
        }
        bussin;
    }

    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_survive()) {
        edgy (b.spawn_t <= 0.0) {
            🚽 Fresh entry into a tremble (fight start, after a bonk, or after
            🚽 a completed charge): flip the sweep direction and arm the tell.
            b.dir     = 0 - b.dir;
            b.spawn_t = t_dindin_tremble();
        }
        b.spawn_t = b.spawn_t - w.dt;
        chad into  = t_dindin_tremble() - b.spawn_t;
        chad grow  = into / t_dindin_tremble();
        chad shake = wave(into * t_dindin_shake_rate())
                     * t_dindin_tremble_shake() * grow;
        🚽 Tremble at the edge he'll charge FROM (opposite the sweep): charging
        🚽 right (+1) => tremble at the left edge, and vice versa, poking
        🚽 t_dindin_peek() px onto the screen so the tell is seen.
        edgy (b.dir > 0) { b.x = t_dindin_peek() - t_dindin_w() + shake; }
        amogus            { b.x = t_screen_w() - t_dindin_peek() + shake; }
        edgy (b.spawn_t <= 0.0) {
            b.phase = t_boss_open();
            edgy (b.dir > 0) { b.x = 0.0 - t_dindin_w(); } 🚽 enter from left
            amogus            { b.x = t_screen_w(); }        🚽 enter from right
        }
        bussin;
    }

    🚽 phase == open: charging across.
    b.x = b.x + b.dir * t_dindin_charge_speed() * w.dt;
    cap gone = L;
    edgy (b.dir > 0 && b.x > t_screen_w()) { gone = W; }
    edgy (b.dir < 0 && b.x < 0.0 - t_dindin_w()) { gone = W; }
    edgy (gone) {
        b.phase   = t_boss_survive();
        b.spawn_t = 0.0; 🚽 fresh tremble on the far side next frame
    }
}

🚽 U Din Din's body hits only a GROUNDED player, and only while charging: a
🚽 low sweep you jump (or bonk). No overhead state, so a jump is always safe --
🚽 the same fairness shape as the shark's low charge, minus the high cross.
cap dindin_contact_hit(gang Boss *b, gang Player *p) {
    edgy (b.phase != t_boss_open()) { bussin L; }
    edgy (!p.grounded) { bussin L; }
    bussin aabb(t_player_x(), p.y, t_player_w(), t_player_h(),
                b.x, t_ground_y() - t_dindin_charge_h(),
                t_dindin_w(), t_dindin_charge_h());
}

🚽 --- La Grande Combinasion (the true final boss, 12.6) -----------------
🚽
🚽 One moveset, run as a small state machine: vanish (OUT) -> a truthful
🚽 destination marker (TELL) -> materialise with the bat up (WIND) -> a low
🚽 forward SWING -> and, once a chain of swings is up, a RECOVERY he can be
🚽 bonked in. The three "phases" are HP-gated: b.bonks 0/1/2 pick tighter
🚽 timings and a longer swing chain before each opening.

🚽 Which phase (0/1/2) the fight is in, by bonks landed.
rizz combi_phase(gang Boss *b) {
    edgy (b.bonks >= 2) { bussin 2; }
    bussin b.bonks;
}

chad combi_tell_time(gang Boss *b) {
    rizz ph = combi_phase(b);
    edgy (ph == 0) { bussin t_combi_tell_a(); }
    edgy (ph == 1) { bussin t_combi_tell_b(); }
    bussin t_combi_tell_c();
}

chad combi_wind_time(gang Boss *b) {
    rizz ph = combi_phase(b);
    edgy (ph == 0) { bussin t_combi_wind_a(); }
    edgy (ph == 1) { bussin t_combi_wind_b(); }
    bussin t_combi_wind_c();
}

chad combi_recover_time(gang Boss *b) {
    rizz ph = combi_phase(b);
    edgy (ph == 0) { bussin t_combi_recover_a(); }
    edgy (ph == 1) { bussin t_combi_recover_b(); }
    bussin t_combi_recover_c();
}

rizz combi_chain(gang Boss *b) {
    rizz ph = combi_phase(b);
    edgy (ph == 0) { bussin t_combi_chain_a(); }
    edgy (ph == 1) { bussin t_combi_chain_b(); }
    bussin t_combi_chain_c();
}

🚽 Choreographed, not random: a deterministic pattern of teleport
🚽 destinations relative to Tung (alternating sides, alternating near/far),
🚽 counted by prev_kind. Clamped so his box lands fully on screen.
skibidi combi_pick_dest(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    rizz n = b.prev_kind;
    b.prev_kind = n + 1;
    rizz side = 1;
    edgy (n % 2 == 0) { side = 0 - 1; }
    chad dist = t_combi_near();
    edgy (n % 4 >= 2) { dist = t_combi_far(); }
    chad want = w.tung_x + side * dist;
    b.dest_x = clampf(want, 40.0, t_screen_w() - t_combi_w() - 40.0);
}

🚽 Lock facing toward Tung. Called ONCE, at materialise: from then the swing
🚽 direction is committed, so a player who runs behind him during the windup
🚽 makes the swing whiff (12.6.3's "get behind him" dodge).
skibidi combi_face(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    edgy (w.tung_x < b.x) { b.dir = 0 - 1; }
    amogus { b.dir = 1; }
}

skibidi combi_move(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    🚽 Beaten: vanish for good, then clear so the win can follow.
    edgy (b.phase == t_boss_leave()) {
        b.state   = t_cs_out();
        b.phase_t = b.phase_t + w.dt;
        edgy (b.phase_t >= 0.6) { boss_clear(b); }
        bussin;
    }

    b.phase_t = b.phase_t + w.dt;

    edgy (b.state == t_cs_out()) {
        edgy (b.phase_t >= t_combi_out_t()) {
            combi_pick_dest(b, w);
            b.state   = t_cs_tell();
            b.phase_t = 0.0;
        }
        bussin;
    }

    edgy (b.state == t_cs_tell()) {
        edgy (b.phase_t >= combi_tell_time(b)) {
            🚽 Materialise EXACTLY on the promised marker, and lock facing.
            b.x       = b.dest_x;
            b.y       = t_ground_y() - t_combi_h();
            combi_face(b, w);
            b.state   = t_cs_wind();
            b.phase_t = 0.0;
        }
        bussin;
    }

    edgy (b.state == t_cs_wind()) {
        edgy (b.phase_t >= combi_wind_time(b)) {
            b.state   = t_cs_swing();
            b.phase_t = 0.0;
        }
        bussin;
    }

    edgy (b.state == t_cs_swing()) {
        edgy (b.phase_t >= t_combi_swing_t()) {
            b.script_i = b.script_i + 1;
            edgy (b.script_i >= combi_chain(b)) {
                🚽 Open the punish window.
                b.script_i = 0;
                b.state    = t_cs_recover();
                b.phase_t  = 0.0;
            }
            amogus {
                🚽 Chain straight into the next teleport -- no opening.
                b.state   = t_cs_out();
                b.phase_t = 0.0;
            }
        }
        bussin;
    }

    🚽 state == recover: hold the opening, then vanish and chain again. A
    🚽 missed opening costs time, not health -- the fight is long, not unfair.
    edgy (b.phase_t >= combi_recover_time(b)) {
        b.state   = t_cs_out();
        b.phase_t = 0.0;
    }
}

🚽 The swing's live hazard: a low band in FRONT of him (the side he faces),
🚽 only while swinging. A jump always clears it -- airborne returns L -- so a
🚽 safe input always exists (the 12.4 invariant, same shape as U Din Din's
🚽 low charge). Reads Tung's real x (p.x), which this fight unpins.
cap combi_contact_hit(gang Boss *b, gang Player *p) {
    edgy (b.state != t_cs_swing()) { bussin L; }
    edgy (!p.grounded) { bussin L; }
    chad hx = b.x;
    chad hw = t_combi_w() + t_combi_swing_reach();
    edgy (b.dir < 0) { hx = b.x - t_combi_swing_reach(); }
    bussin aabb(p.x, p.y, t_player_w(), t_player_h(),
                hx, t_ground_y() - t_combi_swing_h(), hw, t_combi_swing_h());
}

🚽 Bat range for the punish, off Tung's live x (not the pinned constant).
cap combi_in_bat(gang Boss *b, gang Player *p) {
    bussin aabb(p.x + t_hitbox_dx(), p.y + t_hitbox_dy(),
                t_hitbox_w(), t_hitbox_h(),
                b.x, b.y, t_combi_w(), t_combi_h());
}

🚽 Move Tung horizontally, clamped to the arena. Only the Combinasion fight
🚽 calls this; everywhere else his x stays pinned at t_player_x().
skibidi player_move_x(gang Player *p, rizz dir, gang World *w) {
    p.x = p.x + dir * t_combi_run_speed() * w.dt;
    p.x = clampf(p.x, t_combi_arena_l(), t_combi_arena_r() - t_player_w());
    🚽 Ground covered this frame, for the walk cycle (walk_frame).
    p.walk_t = p.walk_t + t_combi_run_speed() * w.dt;
}

cap boss_in_bat(gang Boss *b, gang Player *p) {
    bussin aabb(t_player_x() + t_hitbox_dx(), p.y + t_hitbox_dy(),
                t_hitbox_w(), t_hitbox_h(),
                b.x, b.y, boss_w(b.kind), boss_h(b.kind));
}

🚽 Does the boss's own body overlap the player's?
🚽
🚽 Nothing in the game calls this to deal damage, and that is the point. A
🚽 boss is not dodgeable: the player is pinned at t_player_x() and can only
🚽 jump, so contact damage from a boss that positions itself is damage the
🚽 player cannot avoid. Both bosses' openings used to land on top of Tung
🚽 for exactly that reason -- a heart per opening, three openings to win,
🚽 three hearts.
🚽
🚽 What each boss damages the player WITH is the thing it produces and the
🚽 player can read coming: Tralalero's obstacle barrage, Bombardiro's bombs.
🚽 Those are dodgeable, so those are the fight.
🚽
🚽 This survives as an INVARIANT, asserted over a whole scripted fight in
🚽 test/unit_boss.brainrot: if it is ever true, a boss is standing somewhere
🚽 it must not.
cap boss_hits_body(gang Boss *b, gang Player *p) {
    bussin aabb(t_player_x(), p.y, t_player_w(), t_player_h(),
                b.x, b.y, boss_w(b.kind), boss_h(b.kind));
}

🚽 One bonk per opening: the phase flips away from `open` immediately, so a
🚽 bat that is still out cannot count twice inside the same window.
skibidi boss_take_bonk(gang Boss *b, gang World *w) {
    b.bonks   = b.bonks + 1;
    b.phase_t = 0.0;
    award_bonk(w);
    edgy (b.bonks >= t_boss_bonks()) {
        b.phase = t_boss_leave();
        🚽 Beating a boss is worth more than the three bonks that did it.
        w.bonus = w.bonus + t_boss_reward();
    }
    amogus {
        b.phase = t_boss_survive();
        🚽 Tralalero retreats and re-telegraphs before the next charge, rather
        🚽 than lunging out of the front where the bonk just landed.
        edgy (b.kind == t_boss_tralalero()) { b.spawn_t = t_shark_charge_gap(); }
        🚽 U Din Din: a hit does NOT relocate him into view -- keep him
        🚽 charging (undo the survive flip above) and knock him off the edge he
        🚽 was heading for. dindin_move()'s charge-exit then trembles on the far
        🚽 side and he charges back. Off-screen, so boss_in_bat can't re-bonk.
        edgy (b.kind == t_boss_dimdim()) {
            b.phase = t_boss_open();
            edgy (b.dir > 0) { b.x = t_screen_w() + t_dindin_w(); }
            amogus            { b.x = 0.0 - 2.0 * t_dindin_w(); }
        }
        🚽 La Grande Combinasion: the bonk lands during RECOVERY, so send him
        🚽 straight back out (teleport away) and start the next chain fresh.
        🚽 phase stays `survive` (he keeps owning the spawner) -- combi_move
        🚽 drives everything off b.state.
        edgy (b.kind == t_boss_combinasion()) {
            b.state    = t_cs_out();
            b.phase_t  = 0.0;
            b.script_i = 0;
        }
    }
}

🚽 The gap before the boss's NEXT ground spawn.
🚽
🚽 It exists as a function so the rule is testable. The bug it replaces was
🚽 not a bad constant -- it was main setting `bo.spawn_t = t_boss_gap()`
🚽 directly and never calling fair_clamp() at all, so no constant could have
🚽 saved it. A unit test can call this; it cannot call a line inside main's
🚽 frame loop.
chad boss_spawn_gap(gang Boss *b, rizz kind) {
    bussin fair_clamp(t_boss_gap(), b.prev_kind, kind);
}

🚽 Tralalero closes on every mistake; the croc does not care.
skibidi boss_note_hit(gang Boss *b) {
    edgy (b.kind != t_boss_none()) { b.hits = b.hits + 1; }
}

🚽 --- bombs ---------------------------------------------------------------

🚽 The gravity that makes a bomb take exactly t_bomb_fall_time() to reach
🚽 the ground from the croc's cruising height. Derived rather than tuned:
🚽 the fall TIME is what fairness depends on, so that is the number a human
🚽 sets, and this follows from it. It also avoids needing a square root,
🚽 which math.brainrot does not have.
🚽
🚽 The drop is measured between the two lines bomb_tick() actually uses: the
🚽 bay at the croc's cruising height, and the y at which the shell's own
🚽 bottom edge reaches the ground. It used to subtract t_blast_h() instead of
🚽 t_bomb_h() -- the blast's box, which the shell does not have until after
🚽 it has landed -- so the derived gravity was for a fall 8px shorter than
🚽 the real one and "exactly t_bomb_fall_time()" came out at 1.72s.
chad bomb_gravity() {
    chad from = t_croc_cruise_y() + t_croc_h();
    chad to   = t_ground_y() - t_bomb_h();
    bussin 2.0 * (to - from) / (t_bomb_fall_time() * t_bomb_fall_time());
}

skibidi bomb_spawn(gang Bomb *bm, gang Boss *b) {
    bm.x      = b.x + boss_w(b.kind) * 0.5 - t_bomb_w() * 0.5;
    bm.y      = b.y + boss_h(b.kind);
    bm.vy     = 0.0;
    bm.fall_t = t_bomb_fall_time();
    bm.fuse   = 0.0;
    bm.alive  = W;
}

🚽 Where this bomb is going to land: directly below it.
🚽
🚽 A falling bomb does not scroll. Tung is fixed at t_player_x() and the croc
🚽 is drawn at a screen x, so both are stationary in the camera's frame and
🚽 the croc is flying at exactly Tung's speed. A bomb released from him keeps
🚽 that speed, so in this frame it falls STRAIGHT DOWN. Only once it lands
🚽 does it become part of the world and start scrolling.
🚽
🚽 It used to scroll the whole way down, which was wrong twice over: it made
🚽 the impact point drift by speed * fall_time, and it meant a longer fall
🚽 needed the croc further and further ahead to compensate -- past the right
🚽 edge of the screen at anything over ~1.0s. Falling straight down removes
🚽 that coupling entirely, so the fall time is free to be as generous as it
🚽 needs to be.
🚽
🚽 It is also why a bomb must be released AHEAD of Tung and never over him:
🚽 a column that never changes, against a player who cannot change his, is a
🚽 hit with no input that avoids it. See t_bomb_lead().
chad bomb_landing_x(gang Bomb *bm, gang World *w) {
    bussin bm.x;
}

🚽 A landed bomb is not a second pool -- it is the same slot with a wider
🚽 box and a countdown. `fuse > 0.0` is the whole distinction.
chad bomb_w(gang Bomb *bm) {
    edgy (bm.fuse > 0.0) { bussin t_blast_w(); }
    bussin t_bomb_w();
}

chad bomb_h(gang Bomb *bm) {
    edgy (bm.fuse > 0.0) { bussin t_blast_h(); }
    bussin t_bomb_h();
}

🚽 Falling, then burning. Both states scroll with the world -- a bomb is in
🚽 world space like everything else, so standing still is not a dodge.
🚽 Returns W on the frame the shell detonates (hits the ground), so the
🚽 impact can be heard. False every other frame.
cap bomb_tick(gang Bomb *bm, gang World *w) {
    cap landed = L;
    edgy (bm.fuse > 0.0) {
        🚽 A blast IS part of the world, so it scrolls. A falling bomb is
        🚽 not -- see bomb_landing_x().
        bm.x    = bm.x - w.speed * w.dt;
        bm.fuse = bm.fuse - w.dt;
        edgy (bm.fuse <= 0.0) { bm.alive = L; }
    }
    amogus {
        bm.vy = bm.vy + bomb_gravity() * w.dt;
        bm.y  = bm.y + bm.vy * w.dt;
        bm.fall_t = bm.fall_t - w.dt;
        edgy (bm.fall_t < 0.0) { bm.fall_t = 0.0; }
        edgy (bm.y + t_bomb_h() >= t_ground_y()) {
            🚽 Detonate: the box widens and drops to the ground line, so
            🚽 the blast covers more than the shell that made it.
            bm.y      = t_ground_y() - t_blast_h();
            bm.x      = bm.x + t_bomb_w() * 0.5 - t_blast_w() * 0.5;
            bm.vy     = 0.0;
            bm.fall_t = 0.0;
            bm.fuse   = t_bomb_fuse();
            landed    = W;
        }
    }

    edgy (bm.x < 0.0 - t_blast_w()) { bm.alive = L; }
    bussin landed;
}

cap bomb_hits_player(gang Bomb *bm, gang Player *p) {
    bussin aabb(t_player_x(), p.y, t_player_w(), t_player_h(),
                bm.x, bm.y, bomb_w(bm), bomb_h(bm));
}
